--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0263df275083eba45b37ab9636c8dcbf, type: 3}
  m_Name: MAP-066_Tidal_Reach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mapId: MAP-066
  displayName: Tidal Reach
  environment: Island / Ocean
  warfareFocus: Naval Warfare & Amphibious Operations
  executiveSummary: "Tidal Reach is a tropical island-ocean hybrid battlefield built for naval warfare, amphibious landings, littoral combat, and autonomous multi-domain coordination. The terrain features coral shallows, deep-water channels, sandy beaches, mangrove swamps, cliffside fortifications, island villages, and offshore naval platforms. The map emphasizes autonomous amphibious routing, naval-air coordination, sensor fusion across water and land, and logistics under dynamic tide conditions. In AR, the map anchors at approximately 4\u20135 m viewing distance, covering a 10\xD710 m physical area representing approximately 1 km\xB2. Key features include landing beaches, naval chokepoints, airspace corridors, reef hazards, and combat across sea, air, and land."
  designGoals:
  - name: Naval Warfare in Littoral Waters
    description: Prioritizes ship-to-ship combat, torpedo lanes, reef navigation, and hull-hazard maneuvering. Coral shelves create dynamic cover and movement obstacles.
  - name: Amphibious Operations & Beach Landings
    description: Coordinated landings use amphibious armor, drones, and infantry. Beaches, mangroves, and cliffs create layered defensive zones.
  - name: Air Operations & Reconnaissance
    description: VTOL aircraft, drones, and long-range recon planes operate above the island chain. Airspace corridors between cliffs and offshore platforms define movement and targeting.
  - name: Autonomy & Multi-Domain Coordination
    description: Autonomous units coordinate naval, air, and land forces simultaneously, adapting to shifting tides, fog pockets, and sonar interference.
  - name: Sensor & Information Warfare
    description: Sea spray, humidity, thermal distortion, sonar scatter, and magnetic interference degrade sensors. Cliff relay towers restore clarity; destroying relays creates blind pockets.
  - name: Logistics & Resources
    description: Fuel caches, island depots, and offshore platforms serve as resupply nodes. Convoys must navigate beach approaches and avoid ambush-prone mangrove corridors.
  deployment: Fixed deployment budget of approximately 10,000 points. Blue deploys from the southwest offshore staging platform; Red deploys from the northeast cliffside fortress.
  ar:
    viewingDistance: "~4\u20135 m"
    physicalArea: "10\xD710 m"
    representedArea: "~1 km\xB2 island-ocean zone"
    scale: 1:100
    fov: "~53\xB0 diagonal"
    resolution: "1920\xD71080 per eye"
    tracking: Inside-out tracking detects horizontal planes. Depth mesh, if available, provides limited occlusion.
    interaction: Virtual objects render over the real-world view; assume minimal real-world occlusion.
  coordinateSystem: "1000\xD71000 grid, 1 unit approximately 1 m. Origin (0,0) is the southwest corner."
  keyLocations:
  - name: Blue HQ (Offshore Staging Platform)
    coordinate: (0,0)
    sizeOrElevation: "150\xD7150 m"
    description: Naval docks, drone pads, amphibious armor staging.
  - name: Red HQ (Cliffside Fortress Command)
    coordinate: (1000,1000)
    sizeOrElevation: "150\xD7150 m"
    description: Hardened cliff bunker with radar mast, AA emplacements, and sonar arrays.
  - name: Central Tidal Channel
    coordinate: (500,450)
    sizeOrElevation: "350\xD7250 m"
    description: Deep-water lane, coral shelves, and naval combat zone.
  - name: Island Depot & Village
    coordinate: (250,800)
    sizeOrElevation: "120\xD7120 m"
    description: Supply huts, docks, and interior flanking routes.
  - name: Mangrove Swamp Network
    coordinate: (800,300)
    sizeOrElevation: "200\xD7200 m"
    description: Dense vegetation, shallow water, and stealth movement.
  - name: Landing Beach Corridor
    coordinate: "(0,450 \u2192 400,900)"
    sizeOrElevation: Primary amphibious chokepoint
    description: Layered defenses and tide-driven hazards.
  - name: Cliffside Trail Route
    coordinate: "(300,0 \u2192 450,350)"
    sizeOrElevation: Route
    description: Safer land route with partial cover.
  - name: Cliff Relay A
    coordinate: (650,150)
    sizeOrElevation: +240 m
    description: Long-range sensor vantage point.
  - name: Cliff Relay B
    coordinate: (150,650)
    sizeOrElevation: +260 m
    description: Comms relay hub and sonar control node.
  - name: Neutral Forward Outpost
    coordinate: (500,950)
    sizeOrElevation: Outpost
    description: Drone resupply zone.
  chokepointsAndSightlines:
  - name: Landing Beach Corridor
    description: Major amphibious chokepoint; controlling it determines land access.
  - name: Tidal Channel
    description: Long-range naval and air engagements with dynamic coral cover.
  - name: Mangrove Swamp Network
    description: Interior flanking routes; stealthy but slow.
  - name: Cliffside Trail
    description: Predictable but safe; vulnerable to overwatch from cliffs.
  - name: Sightlines
    description: Cliff Relay A provides long-range sensor coverage of approximately 350 m. Sea spray and humidity create fog-of-war pockets.
  terrain: Beaches, cliffs, coral shelves, mangroves, offshore platforms.
  vegetation: Palm trees, mangroves, shrubs, beach grass.
  buildingsAndProps: 'Military: AA guns, radar dishes, sonar arrays, bunkers. Industrial: docks, generators, pipelines. Logistics: ships, cargo crates, fuel drums, drones.'
  effects: Sea spray, fog, humidity haze, wave impacts, thermal distortion.
  audio: Waves, wind, ship engines, sonar pings, radio chatter.
  lodBudget:
  - category: Coral/Ice/Terrain
    count: 3
    trianglesPerItem: 200000
    totalTriangles: 600000
  - category: Naval/Industrial
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 80000
    totalTriangles: 320000
  - category: Buildings/Military
    count: 15
    trianglesPerItem: 50000
    totalTriangles: 750000
  - category: Roads/Paths
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 30000
    totalTriangles: 120000
  - category: Props
    count: 50
    trianglesPerItem: 10000
    totalTriangles: 500000
  textureBudget: "2048\xB2 for terrain/buildings, 1024\xB2 for props. DXT1/5 compression. Target \u2264100 MB."
  engineAndPlugins: Unreal ARTemplate + Nreal SDK (XREAL). ARKit/ARCore enabled.
  rendering: Forward renderer, stationary lights, baked GI, aggressive culling.
  anchors: Single spatial anchor for entire map.
  interaction: Phone pointer for pan/zoom; HUD as screen-space widgets.
  multiplayer: Client-server architecture; offload AI/physics to server.
  milestones:
  - name: "Prototype Layout \u2014 Month 1"
    description: Block out strait, beaches, mangroves, and test the AR anchor.
  - name: "Core Systems \u2014 Month 2"
    description: NavMesh for sea and land, amphibious autonomy, and air-sea coordination.
  - name: "AR Integration \u2014 Month 3"
    description: Anchors, plane detection, and basic interactivity.
  - name: "Content Fill \u2014 Month 4\u20135"
    description: Final models, textures, lighting, and audio.
  - name: "Gameplay & Polish \u2014 Month 6\u20137"
    description: Objectives, balance, and VFX including sea spray, fog, and thermal distortion.
  - name: "Testing & QA \u2014 Month 8"
    description: Multiplayer stress test and sensor validation.
  testing:
  - name: Autonomy
    description: Verify naval routing, amphibious landings, and air-sea coordination.
  - name: Comms/Sensors
    description: Test relay destruction, fog-of-war updates, and sonar interference.
  - name: Performance
    description: Target at least 60 Hz AR rendering on the target device.
  - name: QA Checklist
    description: Navigation, amphibious logic, deployment budget enforcement, anchor drift, and sensor accuracy.
